{"x": 343.58108085202696, "y": 1374.999999966299, "width": 164.91891891891888, "height": 22.916666666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "tumor necrosis factor (ligand) superfamily, member 6 UDP-glucuronosyltransferase I family, member I", "bbox": {"x": 343.5810772362453, "y": 1402.4999997619047, "width": 503.91891891891896, "height": 55.00000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "apoptosis/necrosis", "bbox": {"x": 952.8648646358107, "y": 1352.0833333031799, "width": 183.24324324324326, "height": 22.916666666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "9.6", "bbox": {"x": 1232.3108102763513, "y": 1347.4999996180554, "width": 41.229729729729684, "height": 22.916666666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "37", "bbox": {"x": 1323.9324322033783, "y": 1347.4999997250002, "width": 32.067567567567615, "height": 27.4999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "NFxB", "bbox": {"x": 1392.6486484195946, "y": 1319.9999999181548, "width": 64.13513513513504, "height": 22.916666666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Apo", "bbox": {"x": 1401.8108105588512, "y": 1352.08333321875, "width": 50.391891891891945, "height": 22.916666666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "GII", "bbox": {"x": 1479.6891889855856, "y": 1319.999999872685, "width": 45.810810810810906, "height": 22.916666666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "F9", "bbox": {"x": 1488.851351168108, "y": 1347.4999997708333, "width": 27.486486486486395, "height": 22.916666666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "TNF ligand family", "bbox": {"x": 952.8648645621862, "y": 1402.499999950893, "width": 169.49999999999997, "height": 27.4999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "DNA damage/repair", "bbox": {"x": 952.3050225893859, "y": 1429.5332342463464, "width": 198.01587713086946, "height": 31.95685714483256}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "12", "bbox": {"x": 1236.891891662838, "y": 1402.4999997250002, "width": 32.067567567567615, "height": 27.4999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "4.6", "bbox": {"x": 1232.3108102763513, "y": 1429.9999996180554, "width": 41.229729729729684, "height": 22.916666666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "8.2", "bbox": {"x": 1319.3513510936657, "y": 1402.4999998567707, "width": 41.229729729729684, "height": 22.916666666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "6.8", "bbox": {"x": 1319.3513511222973, "y": 1434.5833332314812, "width": 41.229729729729684, "height": 18.333333333333513}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Tox Tox", "bbox": {"x": 1401.810810180912, "y": 1402.4999995989583, "width": 50.39189189189175, "height": 55.00000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "HII", "bbox": {"x": 1479.689188960135, "y": 1402.4999998567707, "width": 45.810810810810906, "height": 22.916666666666586}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "CI2", "bbox": {"x": 1479.689188960135, "y": 1429.9999998567707, "width": 45.810810810810906, "height": 22.916666666666828}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "GEArray Q series mouse cDNA gene arrays (SuperArray Bioscience Corporation, Gaithersburg, MD) included the MM-001 cell cycle array (Cycle), MM-002 apoptosis array (Apo), MM-012 stress and toxicity array (Tox) and MM-016 NFXB signaling array (NFKB).", "bbox": {"x": 160.33783761485375, "y": 1494.1666666607587, "width": 1310.1891891891892, "height": 55.00000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "¿Array position, as indicated in Figure 3", "bbox": {"x": 160.33783760878384, "y": 1544.5833333163582, "width": 371.06756756756755, "height": 27.4999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "kinase) and Spp1 (secreted phosphoprotein 1). It further uncovered five genes that were concordantly down regulated: Ak12 (thymoma viral proto-oncogene 2), Bat2 (HLA-B associated transcript 2), Pim 1 (proviral integration site 1), Psmb9 (proteosome subunit, beta type 9) and Sdcl (syndecan 1). One of these genes (Akt2) was included (and also found to be reduced) on the Superarrays, but it failed to reach the confidence criteria for significant change. While a more detailed analysis of the microarray results will be presented in a future publication, these results further strengthened the contention that CDDO-Im", "bbox": {"x": 146.24595940370654, "y": 1608.135576396884, "width": 678.895825875772, "height": 386.2289873758954}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "numerous gene", "bbox": {"x": 462.2531455876597, "y": 1970.290602917034, "width": 216.26856963698933, "height": 32.18461066484441}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "expression", "bbox": {"x": 686.4408329020164, "y": 1968.1998163619337, "width": 139.1281789831213, "height": 32.994933128356884}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "changes, up and down, in the iMyclu-1 and-2 cells.", "bbox": {"x": 146.59459436554056, "y": 2002.916666657184, "width": 673.418918918919, "height": 27.4999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "CDDO-Im decelerates pristane-induced plasmocytomas in", "bbox": {"x": 865.8243239911548, "y": 1608.7499999837964, "width": 668.8378378378378, "height": 32.083333333333464}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "¡MycEs mice", "bbox": {"x": 865.7940346359853, "y": 1640.6985903763139, "width": 142.07409211751582, "height": 32.352819045384805}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The growth inhibiting effects of CDDO-Im in the cell lines indicated that this compound might also inhibit de novo development of Myc-driven B cell and plasma cell tumors in vivo. To evaluate this, we primed congenic BALB/ c.iMych mice with a single i.p. injection of 0.2 ml pristane to undergo inflammation-dependent plasmacytomagenesis in the peritoneal cavity [27]. While only 1 of 14 mice (7.14%) treated with CDDO-Im developed PCT by day 30 of tumor induction, 3 of 11 mice (27.3%) treated with the vehicle control harbored these tumors (Fig. 7 left). A small CDDO-Im-dependent reduction in tumor incidence was", "bbox": {"x": 860.9109650260026, "y": 1668.4825397313534, "width": 683.232670242722, "height": 358.0359379450479}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Page 8 of 15", "bbox": {"x": 1392.54213562854, "y": 2103.1698186744466, "width": 146.80762017739787, "height": 28.660362561543717}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(page number not for citation purposes)", "bbox": {"x": 1195.662161933108, "y": 2135.833332875, "width": 343.58108108108115, "height": 27.4999999999999}}], "ms": 648.482667}